    {
      "id": "clc-feature-dependencies-dependency-resolution-is-only-performed-on-initi-desc-603bcd42",
      "clause": "clu-feature-dependencies-dependency-resolution-is-only-performed-on-initi-desc-603bcd42",
      "disposition": "non-testable",
      "rationale": "States WHEN dependency resolution runs (once, at initial container creation, over the configuration's `features` object) rather than what it produces. The observable consequence of resolving once — re-entering an existing workspace reattaching instead of re-provisioning — is claimed by bhv-up-restart-reuses-container; resolution itself leaves no trace, so 'resolved once' and 'resolved again to the same answer' are indistinguishable on every channel."
